{
  "description": "Determining the protection level of an own-domain name, RELAY-v0.md section 6.5 with the rules of Sections 6.2 and 6.7. Each case: the gateway's ACME account (CAA identity and account URI), the level before, the state of DNSSEC for the zone as the gateway established it (validated: the answers are DNSSEC-validated; unsigned: at least two independent resolvers agree that no DS record exists; bogus: validation fails), and the answers of the resolvers to the queries for CAA at the name. Each resolver has a provider (resolvers of one provider count as one), a status (ok, nxdomain, which is an empty answer, or a failure), the CNAME or DNAME records of the chain at the name or an ancestor, the CAA records at the name (flags, tag, value), and the CAA records at the parent name, which never count. Result: the level, and whether the gateway MUST tell its local administrator because the level fell. Where the zone is unsigned, the answers of all resolvers must be the same in the properties that count (issue and issuewild).",
